/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Divide Two Integers
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Bit Manipulation
Difficulty : Medium

Problem:
Given two integers, divide them without using the
multiplication (*), division (/), or modulus (%) operators.

Return the quotient after truncating the fractional part.
If the result overflows the 32-bit signed integer range,
return INT_MAX.

Approach:
Convert both numbers to their absolute values and repeatedly
subtract the largest possible multiple of the divisor.

Instead of subtracting the divisor one time at a time,
continuously double the divisor until the next doubling would
exceed the remaining dividend. Subtract this largest multiple
and add its corresponding count to the quotient.

Finally, determine the correct sign of the answer.

Why does this work?

Doubling the divisor allows us to remove large portions of the
dividend in every iteration instead of subtracting one divisor
at a time.

This significantly reduces the number of operations while
respecting the restriction of not using multiplication,
division, or modulus operators.

Algorithm:
1. Handle the overflow case.
2. Convert both numbers to positive values.
3. While the dividend is at least the divisor:
   - Double the divisor until it cannot be doubled further.
   - Subtract the largest doubled value.
   - Add its corresponding multiple to the quotient.
4. Apply the correct sign.
5. Return the quotient.

Time Complexity : O(log² n)

Reason:
The outer loop runs O(log n) times, and each iteration may
perform another O(log n) doubling process.

Space Complexity : O(1)

Reason:
Only a constant number of variables are used.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int divide(int dividend, int divisor) {

        // Handle the overflow case.
        if (dividend == INT_MIN && divisor == -1) {
            return INT_MAX;
        }

        if (dividend == INT_MIN && divisor == 1) {
            return INT_MIN;
        }

        // Convert both numbers to positive values.
        long long absoluteDividend = abs((long long)dividend);
        long long absoluteDivisor = abs((long long)divisor);

        int quotient = 0;

        // Compute the quotient.
        while (absoluteDividend >= absoluteDivisor) {

            long long currentSum = absoluteDivisor;
            long long currentCount = 1;

            // Keep doubling until the next doubling exceeds
            // the remaining dividend.
            while (currentSum <= absoluteDividend - currentSum) {
                currentSum += currentSum;
                currentCount += currentCount;
            }

            absoluteDividend -= currentSum;
            quotient += currentCount;
        }

        // Apply the correct sign.
        if ((dividend < 0) ^ (divisor < 0)) {
            return -quotient;
        }

        return quotient;
    }
};
